Message-ID: <alpine.WNT.1.10.1402241443390.2856@morrism-PC>

Sanne,

You should adjust for network size using the offset described in Pavel 
Krivitsky's paper
http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1572312711000086

This addresses a different issue, which concerns the question of whether 
density or mean degree is preserved as network size changes.  The 
adjustment describe in that paper makes it possible to compare the 
coefficients of dyadic-independent terms across networks (as long as the 
models are the same).  If you have dyadic-dependent terms in the model 
(like gwesp or degree terms) this simple offset does not solve the problem 
for those coefficients.  But Pavel presented some new work at the Sunbelt 
last week on this topic.

hope this helps,
Martina


