Dear statnet users,

I have a question regarding the analysis of an observed network with ~100
nodes using ergm.  In addition to other parameters, I would like to include
a continuous node level attribute as a term in my model (using nodecov).
The issue is that this term is not linear and would be better fit by a
quadratic parameter (i.e. high probability of tie formation at either small
or large values of the attribute, low probability at middle values).

