Dear Statnet Help List,

I'd like to follow up on a question that I asked last week about using
offset to address the problem of structural zeros.  I am getting the
following error:

Error in ergm(dind, estimate = "MPLE", constraints = constraints,
eval.loglik = FALSE,  :
  Invalid offset parameter vector offset.coef: wrong number of parameters:
expected 1 got 2.

Looking at the ergm source code, this error occurs whenever:

length(offset.coef) is not equal to
length(control$init[model.initial$etamap$offsettheta])

More specifically, ergm is telling me that length(offset.coef)=2, but it
should equal 1.

It is beyond my understanding how the length of offset.coef got to be 2,
since I set it at offset.coef=-Inf.  I have also tried offset.coef=0 and
offset.coef=1, but they yield the same error.  Looking at the ergm source
code, it seems that offset.coef is something that is set by me -- it does
not seem to be determined endogenously.  But, obviously, something is
happening to offset.coef that is extending the length of the vector.

What, if anything, can I do to fix the problem?  Is my problem an
estimation problem or a programming problem?

