Message-ID: <alpine.WNT.1.10.1407111400170.6952@morrism-PC>

Say your population is size 100.

In the degree distribution for this population, each tie will be nominated 
twice (once by each partner).  So if you count the number of ties as

num ties = sum(degree * number of persons with that degree)

You will double count the number of ties.

That's why we divide by two in the mixing matrix, since the mixing matrix 
is a crosstabulation of the number of ties.


