Sorry -- hit send too quickly.  What I meant to say was:

Say your population is size 100, and everyone has one tie to someone else 
in the population.  If you survey all of the nodes, and ask about their 
ties (like you do in an egocentric sample), you'll get 100 reported ties. 
But each tie is reported twice, once by each person, so in the population 
there are, in fact, only 50 ties.


