Ya,

A close cousin to statnet and friends is the "igraph" package in R (and 
Python).  A book that describes this package's functionality, including 
ergm and a few of the statnet functions, is:

Kolaczyk, E. and Csardi, G. (2014), Statistical Analysis of Network Data 
with R, Springer.

This is more of a professional reference book than a scholarly text, 
although it's well-referenced.  I can commend this book highly to you.

