2. Second- while the second set of results above seem reasonable- they?re not exactly accurate. Specifically, this network has 13,476 men, 11,524 women, and 17,971 female/male ties. So by my calculation- if we impose the above restrictions (i.e. assume only female/male ties are possible)- the edges coefficient should be -9.064, not -10.457. Such miscalculations occur elsewhere as well- see, for instance, the following model run in statnet compared to an equivalent estimation in Stata (where Stata produces the correct results). Note: Interestingly, though the parameter estimates are wrong, the standard errors are actually quite close. This happens elsewhere as well.

