Hi everyone,

I'm trying to use the gof.ergmm function from the latentnet package, and it
seems to be creating unexpectedly large gofobject objects, which is causing
problems when I'm trying to save a goodness of fit object from several
networks.  Does anyone know why, or how to fix it?  I've included more
detail, and a possible partial solution below.

Here's an example:

> rm(list = ls())> library(statnet)> > # Library for memory use; see http://adv-r.had.co.nz/memory.html> library(pryr)> > data(sampson)> samp.fit <- ergmm(samplike ~ euclidean(d = 2))> > samp.gof <- gof(samp.fit)> object_size(samp.gof)6.98 MB

Running gof.ergmm on the example from the documentation gives a 7MB file.
For a single network, this isn't a huge problem -- my computer isn't
choking on 7MB -- but it becomes a problem when you try to loop over many
model fits, for many networks.

My best guess is that R is doing a poor job of garbage collection at the
end of the gof.ergmm function.  The gof.ergmm function simulates several
networks from the model fit, and then calculates statistics using those.
When it's done, it doesn't seem to return the memory used by the
simulations.  Adding a rm(SimNetworkSeriesObj) statement in the function
seems to produce much smaller gofobject objects, presumably because then R
returns the memory used by the simulations.  Code for this is below
(apologies for the length -- I copied and pasted the gof.ergmm function).

> # Set up workspace> rm(list = ls())> library(statnet)> > # Library for memory use; see http://adv-r.had.co.nz/memory.html> library(pryr)> > # Modified GOF object> newGOF <- function (object, ..., nsim = 100, GOF = ~idegree + odegree + +                            distance, verbose = FALSE) + {+   formula <- object[["model"]][["formula"]]+   trms <- ergm.getterms(formula)+   if (length(trms) > 2) {+     nw <- eval(trms[[2]], sys.parent())+   }+   else {+     stop("A network object on the RHS of the formula argument must be given")+   }+   nsim <- max(nsim, dim(object[["Z"]])[3])+   all.gof.vars <- all.vars(GOF)+   for (i in seq(along = all.gof.vars)) {+     all.gof.vars[i] <- match.arg(all.gof.vars[i], c("distance", +                                                     "espartners", "dspartners", "odegree", "idegree", +                                                     "degree", "triadcensus", "model"))+   }+   GOF <- as.formula(paste("~", paste(all.gof.vars, collapse = "+")))+   if (!is.network(nw)) {+     stop("A network object on the RHS of the formula argument must be given")+   }+   pval.model <- pval.triadcensus <- pval.dist <- pval.deg <- pval.espart <- pval.espart <- NULL+   obs.model <- pobs.model <- sim.model <- psim.model <- pval.model <- bds.model <- NULL+   obs.triadcensus <- pobs.triadcensus <- sim.triadcensus <- psim.triadcensus <- pval.triadcensus <- bds.triadcensus <- NULL+   obs.dist <- pobs.dist <- sim.dist <- psim.dist <- pval.dist <- bds.dist <- NULL+   obs.deg <- pobs.deg <- sim.deg <- psim.deg <- pval.deg <- bds.deg <- NULL+   obs.espart <- pobs.espart <- sim.espart <- psim.espart <- pval.espart <- bds.espart <- NULL+   obs.dspart <- pobs.dspart <- sim.dspart <- psim.dspart <- pval.dspart <- bds.dspart <- NULL+   obs.ideg <- pobs.ideg <- sim.ideg <- psim.ideg <- pval.ideg <- bds.ideg <- pval.ideg <- NULL+   obs.odeg <- pobs.odeg <- sim.odeg <- psim.odeg <- pval.odeg <- bds.odeg <- pval.odeg <- NULL+   n <- network.size(nw)+   if ("model" %i