based on the same data with the same formula (except for the additional 
endogenous model terms in the ERGM case and the euclidean distance 
parameter in the latent space model). I tend to think that all three 
models should return fairly similar results, but this is apparently not 
the case: the ERGM and the QAP model look pretty similar, but the latent 
space model has some coefficients which are significant in the opposite 
direction. I'd like to learn more about where it's going wrong. Any 
ideas or suggestions on what I could try? Here is a results table for 
the three models:

